---
title: "Collections and indexes"
description: "Define Qdrant collection topology, payload indexes, and custom shard keys from QQL."
sidebar:
  order: 5
---

Collection declarations make vector topology reviewable alongside the queries
that use it. Define vectors first, add payload indexes for fields you filter or
order by, and add shard keys only when Qdrant routing is part of the design.

## Model the vector topology

Vector names are application-defined. `dense`, `bm25`, and `colbert` are useful
conventions, but vector configuration determines the actual role.

{% qqlExample title="Dense, sparse, and multivector topology" %}
```sql
CREATE COLLECTION research (
  dense VECTOR(384, COSINE),
  bm25 SPARSE,
  colbert VECTOR(128, COSINE)
    WITH MULTIVECTOR (comparator = 'max_sim')
    WITH HNSW (m = 0)
)
WITH HNSW (
  m = 16,
  ef_construct = 100
);
```
{% /qqlExample %}

| Requirement | Schema choice |
|---|---|
| Semantic retrieval | A dense `VECTOR(size, distance)` |
| Lexical or sparse retrieval | A named `SPARSE` vector |
| Late interaction | A multivector with a comparator |
| Hybrid retrieval | Both a dense and sparse vector |

## Index the filter paths you use

Create payload indexes for fields used frequently in filters, tenant predicates,
or ordering. Index design is a Qdrant performance decision, not a requirement
for every payload field.

{% qqlExample title="Tenant and text payload indexes" %}
```sql
CREATE INDEX ON COLLECTION research
FOR tenant_id
TYPE keyword
WITH (
  is_tenant = true,
  on_disk = true
);

CREATE INDEX ON COLLECTION research
FOR content
TYPE text
WITH (
  tokenizer = 'multilingual',
  lowercase = true,
  phrase_matching = true
);
```
{% /qqlExample %}

## Route a collection with custom shard keys

Shard-key DDL creates and manages routing partitions. It is separate from the
tenant predicate your service must enforce.

{% qqlExample title="Manage a custom shard key" %}
```sql
CREATE SHARD KEY 'acme'
ON COLLECTION research
WITH (shards_number = 2);

SHOW SHARD KEYS
ON COLLECTION research;

DROP SHARD KEY 'acme'
ON COLLECTION research;
```
{% /qqlExample %}

{% aside type="note" title="Remote-backend capability" %}
Shard-key DDL is a Qdrant remote-backend capability. The in-process edge backend
does not support shard keys, `ALTER COLLECTION`, or grouped queries.
{% /aside %}

